      "unit": "U2",
      "test": "core/internal/session/store_test.go — what the core writes to the sessions and connections buckets validates against continuity-state.schema.json"
    }
  ],
  "description": "The durable state a restarted core reattaches from (Storage §8.6; immortality §7): the sessions bucket holds the record E0 already writes, and an E0-written record loads unchanged — the migration-free rule plan.md §3 sets for C6: its owner_id and tenant_id are \"\" and its two clocks carry the process's local offset. A v0.2 core writes the clocks in UTC with Z, and adds protocol and out_bytes_committed. recording_last_seq_out is immortality §4.1's last_committed_seq — one counter, never a renamed copy beside it — and unreachable_reason lives only in the nested northbound record. The connections bucket maps a connection to its worker, target, credential reference, version and sessions, and keeps the buffer_bytes and input_frame_max it was connected with — fixed for the connection's life — so a restarted core splits input at the value the worker holds, never at a value its configuration now has. What is refused: a second counter, a second unreachable_reason, a clock with no zone, an ended_at not in UTC, and any field the layout does not hold.",
  "corpus": [
    "Storage §8.6",
    "Storage §9",
    "immortality §4.1",
    "immortality §7",
    "plan.md §3 C6",
    "decision 5.39"
  ],
